{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MarkovZFullBarCondition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovZFullBarCondition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ZBarParity","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceTLUniqueness"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.decayLadder_zC_threeRow_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.decayLadder_zC_threeRow_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZFullBarCondition.lean#L200-L227","doc":"**Mutual exclusivity: the C-frame decay ladder and the two-row forcing.**\nANY faithful normalised Markov trace on `H₃(q)` (the three Markov equations\nagainst the `H₃(q)` character table, `y_(2,1) ≠ 0`) whose Ocneanu parameter is\nthe decay ladder's `z_C` (`z·(s + s⁻¹) = 1`, `q = s²`, `s > 1`) carries a\nNONZERO three-row weight `y_(1³)` — it does not factor through Temperley–Lieb.\n\nConsequence for bean `qou-b3nk`: the mass channel's forcing\n(`y_(1³) = 0 ⟹ z = z_D`, `markovWeights_eq_jones_of_threeRow_eq_zero`) cannot\n\"transfer\" to the Q_β channel while the ladder keeps `z_C` — if the decay\ndecomposition kills the third row, the decay trace is `z_D` and the existing\nC-frame ladder is not that trace (re-derivation, not substitution); if the\nladder's parameter is retained, the third row is forcibly present.  Which horn\nis the decay channel's is NOT decided here: no corpus block derives the decay\nfibre, and the channel is registered `disputed`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.decayLadder_zC_not_jones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.decayLadder_zC_not_jones","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZFullBarCondition.lean#L168-L198","doc":"**The decay ladder's parameter fails the Jones/TL pin.**  For `s > 1`, a\nparameter `z` with `z·(s + s⁻¹) = 1` (i.e. `z = z_C = 1/(√q + 1/√q)`, the\nvalue hard-coded in `qbeta_utils.markov_parameter` and the KC21/KC22 ladder\ncore) does NOT satisfy `z·[2]_q = q²` (`q = s²`).  Denominator-cleared, the\ncoincidence locus is `s⁷ + s⁵ = s⁴ + 1`, which is impossible for `s > 1`\n(each `s > 1` has `s⁷ > s⁴` and `s⁵ > 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zC_fails_fullBar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zC_fails_fullBar","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZFullBarCondition.lean#L145-L166","doc":"**`z_C` fails the full-bar condition on the substrate side.**  In the\nhalf-power coordinate `s = √q` with `s > 1` (every substrate anchor has\n`q > 1`):  `bar(z_C) ≠ z_C − h`, written out with `bar` acting as `s ↦ s⁻¹`\nand `h = q − q⁻¹ = s² − s⁻²`.  Uses `z_bar_invariant_field` (bar-evenness of\n`z_C`); the failure is then exactly `h ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.eigenphase_bar_defect_of_fullBar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.eigenphase_bar_defect_of_fullBar","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZFullBarCondition.lean#L126-L139","doc":"**Full-bar parameter ⟹ eigenphase bar defect exactly `h²`.**  If instead\n`bar(z) = z − h` (the full-bar condition, which `z_D` satisfies and a bar-even\n`z` cannot away from `q² = 1` — `barEven_fullBar_forces_classical`), then\n`bar(2α) + 2α = h²` rather than `0`.\n\nSo the failure is not a perturbation to be estimated: it is an exact,\n`z`-independent remainder.  Every parameter satisfying the full-bar condition\nhas the SAME defect, so no choice within that family restores bar-oddness. The\nbar-odd projection of the D-frame eigenphase is therefore `α − h²/4`\n(undoubled), which is a derived correction carrying no free parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.eigenphase_barOdd_of_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.eigenphase_barOdd_of_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZFullBarCondition.lean#L117-L124","doc":"**Bar-even parameter ⟹ bar-ODD eigenphase.**  With `bar(h) = −h` (immediate\nfrom `h = q − q⁻¹`), a bar-even `z` makes `2α = (z−1)h` bar-odd:\n`bar(2α) + 2α = 0`.  This is the convention-C case, and it is the hypothesis\n`eigenphase_bar_involution` encodes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.barEven_fullBar_forces_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.barEven_fullBar_forces_classical","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZFullBarCondition.lean#L85-L93","doc":"**A bar-EVEN Markov parameter satisfies the full-bar condition only at the\nclassical point.**  If `bar(z) = z` (convention C's property, proved for\n`z_C = √q/(1+q)` in `ZBarParity.z_bar_invariant`) and `bar(z) = z − (q − qi)`\n(the full-bar condition), then `q² = 1`.  Contrapositive: away from `q² = 1`,\nconvention C fails the full-bar condition — the exact reverse of the\ncoefficient-half verdict that had been read as favouring C. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zD_full_bar_covariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zD_full_bar_covariant","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZFullBarCondition.lean#L74-L83","doc":"**`bar(z_D) = z_D − h`, division-free.**  With `q⁻¹` carried as `qi`\n(`q·qi = 1`), the cross-multiplied form of\n`qi³/(qi²+1) = q³/(q²+1) − (q − qi)`:  both sides equal `1/(q³+q)` as\nfractions, and the identity below is their denominator-cleared form.  This is\nthe z-level content of \"convention D's Markov trace commutes with the full bar\ninvolution at the stabilisation step\" — the trace-level premise\n(`tr∘bar = bar∘tr`) is NOT proved here. ","signatureChunk":0}]}